id: og_drydock_b
name: Dry Dock II
description: Dry Dock. A drained dock with a quay all the way round it, where crossing on the quay means being seen from everywhere and the only alternative is the pump gallery beneath. Built as a ship repair dock; the dock was pumped down for survey and the caisson has not been floated back.

